SWEET WLAN keep events (patch 0281, W-D6 boot A, branch wlan/rejoin; docs/research/W-D6-rejoin-dhcp.md): the keep phase no longer consumes WL_EVENT items unread. (1) Every ring-2 item of type 0xE is decoded (sweet_wlan_g2.h swg_ke_event, the frame parse factored out of swg_e_event into the pure swg_e_fparse) and printed as ONE line `SWEET WLAN: keep event type T flags F status S reason R auth A datalen D item_len L` (no address, no ifname); an unknown or short frame is a `WIFI GAP: keep event ...` line. (2) The consumed event buffer is re-posted under a fresh pktid (swg_ke_flush: the existing swg_d4d_post store kind, ten item words + H2D-WR slot + doorbell 0, judged by the L25 whitelist as class L2 buffer post, L7 index, L9 doorbell, as Linux msgbuf.c and OpenBSD if_bwfm_pci.c do for every event), after the ring-2 read-index update; events that arrive inside the RSSI refresh ioctl go the same way (swg_e_items keep branch) and the refresh drains ring 2 first (swl25_rssi_drain) so a busy ring 2 no longer skips every refresh. (3) Link-down detector (swg_ke_note): LINK with flag 0x01 clear, DEAUTH 5, DEAUTH_IND 6, DISASSOC 11, DISASSOC_IND 12 or SET_SSID with a non-zero status take UP -> DOWN exactly once (`SWEET WLAN: keep link DOWN cause C status S reason R`); a link-up event while DOWN is logged and the state stays DOWN (UP needs a new 4-way, patch 0282). WLC_GET_RSSI = 0 is logged as a hint only. (4) On DOWN the keep thread (this patch, bsd/dev/sweet_wlan.c) tells iOS and sends NOTHING to the firmware: sweet_wlan_a80211_kept_link(0) clears kept.joined (swr_kept_clear) and fires SWSTA_REV_LINK_DOWN (wifid gets LINK_CHANGED isLinkDown 1; a join of the kept SSID now fails), en0_link_only(e, 0) turns IFF_RUNNING off and posts KEV_DL_LINK_OFF without failing the flow ring. (5) DHCP credentials: a credential blob with ip == 0 AND gw == 0 runs the join and the 4-way as before and skips L26 (`SWEET WLAN: L26 not run: DHCP credentials (no static address)`); exactly one of the two zero stays refused. The headers (sweet_wlan_g2.h, sweet_wlan_l25_hs.h, sweet_wlan_l25_glue.h, sweet_wlan_radio.h, sweet_wlan_en0.h, sweet_wlan_a80211.c) are regenerated in place in patches 0174, 0206, 0199 and 0201 from shim/ (tools/gen-wlan-hunks, tools/gen-wlan-en0-patch, tools/gen-wlan-a80211-patch), as for 0273; this patch holds the hand-written glue hunks of sweet_wlan.c. New firmware-facing stores: only the event-buffer re-post above (existing store kind, existing whitelist classes). Not run on hardware.
